cff-version: 1.2.0
title: A 90% ECG threshold does not hold at another hospital or in another care setting
message: If you use this repository, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abbou
    given-names: Ruben
repository-code: https://github.com/rabbou/ecg-conformal-shift
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Measures how many of the ill an ECG cut-off set to catch 90% at one place
  catches once it is used unchanged on other patients. Myocardial infarction
  cut-offs set on PTB-XL are carried to hospitals in Shandong and Chongqing;
  five collections take turns setting cut-offs for sinus rhythm, atrial
  fibrillation, left and right bundle-branch block and first-degree
  atrioventricular block; and structural heart disease cut-offs set on
  Columbia inpatients in EchoNext are carried to its outpatients, for four
  models. A single cut-off answering yes or no is compared with conformal
  prediction, which refers patients in a grey zone to a doctor, its edges set
  for all patients together or for the ill and the healthy separately. The
  study reports how many patients each option refers, what the AUROC and the
  share referred show without known diagnoses, and how many local ECGs with
  known diagnoses restore the share caught.
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - electrocardiography
  - structural heart disease
  - myocardial infarction
  - distribution shift
  - class-conditional coverage
